    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/helsinki-Project-Manager-Innovation-Unit/1373564057/": {
      "title": "Open position",
      "description": "Project Manager / Innovation Unit Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Project Manager / Innovation Unit The University of Helsinki is strengthening its innovation activities and the societal impact of research. Our strategic priorities include increasing RDI collaboration with companies, supporting the creation of new student- and research-driven companies, developing open research infrastructures and experimentation environments, and strengthening the university’s innovation culture. The University of Helsinki is seeking a Project Manager to join the Innovation Unit within University Services. Role is fixed-term position until 31.10.2028. About the role: Your main responsibility will be to act as the Project Manager for the University of Helsinki’s part of the Helsinki+Espoo+Vantaa Innovations (HEVi) DualBoost -project (Dual-Use Technology Ecosystem Development in the Capital Region). A key part of your role will be to develop projects funded through external sources (e.g. NATO, the European Defence Fund, and Business Finland), focusing on dual-use innovation activities, Startup & SME collaboration, and ecosystem development, in cooperation with university researchers and external partners. Your responsibilities will include active development of project ideas, building and coordinating consortia, and leading collaborative project development. You will also be responsible for reporting on and monitoring the finances of the University of Helsinki’s share of the project. As part of your role, you will build stakeholder relationships and participate in key dual-use networks. Success in the role will be demonstrated through new partnerships, externally funded collaborative projects, and a more active role for the University of Helsinki in key dual-use technology networks. The position requires strong knowledge of funding instruments, particularly the European Defence Fund (EDF), as well as practical experience in developing and building projects. The role involves working extensively across innovation projects and collaboration activities on the University of Helsinki’s different campuses. A broad understanding of the university’s diverse research areas will be an advantage in succeeding in the role. You are comfortable building new collaborations and enjoy working with stakeholder relations. Knowledge, experience and networks in the (Finnish) defence ecosystem are a benefit. Expertise related to innovation activities and university–industry collaboration — including research collaboration, innovation ecosystems, development and experimentation environments, innovation and research infrastructures, commercialisation, education, and research — will be considered an advantage. Project development and proposal preparation will primarily be conducted in English, and successful performance in the role requires fluent written and spoken English. Existing extensive international networks in relevant fields will also be considered an advantage. Successful performance in the role requires the ability to work independently, a strong vision and expertise in building competitive project concepts, an interest in engaging with a wide range of subject areas, and the ability to develop project collaboration across the university research community and with external partners. What we offer: You will become part of our skilled team, to which you will contribute your expertise and your own personality. We offer an interesting and varied role with opportunities to develop your skills. The University of Helsinki is a responsible employer, where achieving a good work-life balance is a key priority. We look after your wellbeing and ensure your day-to-day life runs smoothly through, for example, flexible working hours, annual leave entitlements exceeding the statutory minimum, comprehensive occupational health services and Unisport’s wide range of sports facilities. At the University, we work in a hybrid model, combining remote and on-site work. A sense of community is one of our core values, which is why we also want to meet in person on campus. It is important to us to ensure a flexible balance between work and leisure time. Interested? Apply for the role via the link below by 19 October 2026 at the latest. Please, include your CV and a cover letter in which you outline your motivation and experience in your own words. For further information, please contact Kalle Toivonen by email: kalle.toivonen@helsinki.fi A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to us. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply for our positions. Click this link to read about accessibility and inclusivity at our University. JOIN US TO BUILD A BETTER WORLD – TOGETHER! #HelsinkiUniCareers Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 19.10.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: University Services Sub-unit: Financial Services ID: 5240 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Leadership specialist and support positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of 