    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Strategy-Director/1373702457/": {
      "title": "Strategy Director",
      "description": "Strategy Director Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Strategy Director We are seeking an experienced STRATEGY DIRECTOR for the University of Helsinki, with a strong understanding of the higher education and academic sectors. You will support the University’s management in shaping the future direction of its operations and achieving its strategic objectives, as well as to lead the strategic management support services. About the role As Strategy Director, you will work as a partner to the Rector's of the University of Helsinki and other University management. You will help the management team to develop a shared, forward-looking view of the situation, make decisions and lead strategic projects. You will be responsible for preparing the strategy process and supporting its implementation across the entire university. You will lead the University’s strategic management and operational management support services together with your team’s Planning Manager and four Strategy Managers. You will support the leaders of the University and its faculties, as well as the organisation as a whole, in strategic work, annual operational management, and the analysis of operations and forecasting the future. Your team leads the provision of strategic management support across four campuses in a matrix structure. As Strategy Director, you are responsible for ensuring that these strategic management services provide effective support for the university’s impactful leadership and also meet future needs. As Strategy Director, you will work within the General Administration division, reporting to the Director of Administration, and will be a member of the University Services Management Team. This is a permanent position, commencing on 1 January 2027 or as otherwise agreed. What do we expect from you? You are an experienced leader with a strong understanding of strategic management, organisational development and the use of data in decision-making. You act naturally as a partner to senior management and are able to analyse complex issues, challenge prevailing views where necessary, and assist management in making decisions. You understand the university and its operating environment as a whole within a global context. You have a proven track record in strategic work, are familiar with the tools and processes of effective strategic work, and have a proven track record of leading large-scale development projects. You lead your team leaders in a goal-oriented manner and support their development. We particularly value: Experience and a proven track record in visionary strategy and development work Experience in change management, as well as a proven track record and results from successful change management. The ability to utilise and analyse information to support foresight, decision-making and practical operations. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, as well as the ability to build collaboration across team and organisational boundaries. Experience of working in international and culturally diverse organisations. A relevant higher education degree is required; a PhD is considered an advantage. Proficiency in Finnish, Swedish and English is required. The University will support the successful candidate in improving their Finnish language skills during the first year, if necessary. Why the University of Helsinki? The University of Helsinki is Finland’s leading and internationally renowned research university. As Director of Strategy, you will help shape the university’s future and strengthen the role of strategic management in the university’s operations. You will lead a team of experienced experts and work in close collaboration with the university’s management, faculties and university services. You will carry out work that has a significant impact on society as part of an internationally renowned academic community. Interested? Recruitment is being carried out in collaboration with Sari Salojärvi of IMS Talent. You can contact her directly by email to arrange a telephone interview: sari.salojarvi@imstalent.com If you wish to apply for the role directly, you can do so via the application link by 26 October 2026 at the latest. Please upload your CV and cover letter, including your salary expectations, to the system. Please highlight why you are the right person for the role of Strategy Director and provide examples in your application of successful change management or strategic leadership. Please note that recruitment at the University of Helsinki is public. A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to us. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply for our positions. Click this link to read about accessibility and inclusivity at our University. JOIN US TO BUILD A BETTER WORLD – TOGETHER! #HelsinkiUniCareers Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 26.10.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: University Services Sub-unit: Administrative Services ID: 5243 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Leadership specialist and support positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose 