    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Research-assistant-in-Faculty-of-Law/1375232557/": {
      "title": "Research assistant in Faculty of Law",
      "description": "Research assistant in Faculty of Law Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research assistant in Faculty of Law The Faculty of Law at the University of Helsinki is seeking 1–2 Research Assistants for a fixed‑term position of 1 year with the possibility for extension, starting at the earliest in December 2026, latest January 2027. The Research Assistant will work across several research projects and initiatives, including: Agency in Law (LEGACY), examining changing forms of legal agency from the perspective of legal theory, including persons with intellectual disabilities, artificial intelligence systems, and animals as agents HUMAN-BIO, investigating alternatives to animal experimentation, An upcoming project examining the legal status of AI systems and the problem of digital minds, and Helsinki Animal Law Centre, one of the largest academic hubs for animal law research globally The Research Assistant’s duties will include various supporting tasks, such as: communicating about the activities and events of the research projects (including social media, website, and email communications) assisting with the organization of events assisting with research-related work, often involving the finalization, proofreading, and editing of documents providing other practical and administrative assistance to the research projects and research groups The position requires: a proactive and creative approach to updating the social media channels and websites of the research projects strong practical organizational skills a basic understanding of how academic research works good command of spoken and written English a positive, solution-oriented attitude The following are considered an advantage: experience organizing events good command of Finnish an interest in legal theory, animal law and ethics, artificial intelligence, or related topics familiarity with graphic design tools (for example, Canva) other language skills We may hire two research assistants with complementary strengths, so we don’t necessarily expect any single applicant to meet every criterion. We do, however, aim to hire at least one assistant with strong social media and communications skills. We offer an opportunity to become part of a world-class research environment and to participate in international academic activities and events. Our research groups operate primarily in English, and a good command of English is therefore essential. As the work involves practical arrangements at the University of Helsinki, it cannot be performed entirely remotely. The Research Assistant must be an undergraduate or Master’s-level student at the University of Helsinki. The position is part-time, approximately 5–20 hours per week. It may be combinable with a summer job, as long as the assistant is able to assist with certain events planned for the summer of 2027. So far, such events are planned for June 16-18 and June 21-23, 2027. The hourly salary is 16,04 – 17,03 EUR, depending on previous work experience. Please submit your application through the recruitment system by November 2, 2026 via the \"Apply Now\" button. Attach the following to your application: Motivation letter (or explanation of motivation in the application letter) CV Transcript of academic records Please log into our recruitment system using your personal email address (not an @helsinki.fi address). For questions concerning the position, please contact Visa Kurki at visa.kurki(at)helsinki.fi. For questions related to the recruitment system, please reach out to recruitment@helsinki.fi You may also contact the current Research Assistant, Amanda Vilén, at amanda.vilen@helsinki.fi The University of Helsinki encourages applicants from a diverse range of genders, age groups, language and cultural backgrounds, as well as minorities. You can read about our university's accessibility and inclusivity from this link: Accessibility Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 2.11.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Faculty of Law Sub-unit: Faculty of Law ID: 5277 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Leadership specialist and support positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising Cookies Provider Description Enabled Google Tag Manager Google Tag Manager is a tag management system for conversion tracking, site analytics, remarketing and more. Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleTagManager Google Analytics Google Analytics is a web analytics service offered by Google that tracks and reports website traffic. Cookie Information Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider GoogleAnalytics LinkedIn LinkedIn is an employment-oriented social networking service. We use the Apply with LinkedIn feature to allow you to apply for jobs using your LinkedIn profile. Opting out of LinkedIn cookies will disable your ability to use Apply with LinkedIn. Cookie Policy Cookie Table Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider LinkedIn Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
