    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Doctoral-researcher-in-computational-genomics-for-predictive-medicine/1374865857/": {
      "title": "Doctoral researcher in computational genomics for predictive medicine",
      "description": "Doctoral researcher in computational genomics for predictive medicine Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Doctoral researcher in computational genomics for predictive medicine Doctoral researcher in computational genomics for predictive medicine The Barrett lab at the University of Helsinki is recruiting a doctoral researcher (PhD student) in computational genomics for predictive medicine. We are jointly affiliated with the ELLIS Institute Finland , the Institute for Molecular Medicine Finland (FIMM) , and the Faculty of Medicine at the University of Helsinki. We analyze multiomic data to discover, understand, and measure mechanistically meaningful subtypes of complex human diseases. We believe that characterizing diseases not by their observed clinical phenotype, but by their molecular and biological endotype, will enable better treatment for patients. This long-held ambition in biomedicine is now poised to be realized due to: •    National research biobanks that collectively include millions of individuals with matched biosamples and detailed electronic health records. •    Large and growing multiomic data sets in samples from these biobanks, including genomics, proteomics, metabolomics, and transcriptomics. •    New machine learning and AI methods to build multiomic models that stratify disease risk, progression, and treatment response by molecular endotypes. Find examples of research areas and possible projects on our website. Responsibilities •    Design and implement a PhD research project on a topic related to computational genomics for predictive medicine. •    Carry out the research project: propose hypotheses, write code, think about and discuss results, and interpret findings. •    Collaborate closely with other members of the team, other researchers at the ELLIS Institute and University of Helsinki, and international partners. •    Share scientific results via publications and presentations at local and international conferences, and contribute more broadly to open science (e.g. via pre-prints and open source software). •    Contribute to mentoring and training the next generation of scientists. Qualifications, experience, and skills These items are most important for this role. We expect candidates to fulfill most of these: •    Motivation to work collaboratively on hard scientific problems with a pragmatic focus on getting things done. •    Master’s degree in computational biology, data science, bioinformatics, or a related discipline (exceptional candidates may be considered coming straight from a bachelor’s). •    Proficiency in programming for data analysis in either Python or R. •    Research experience in computational biology and/or data science. •    Excellent written and spoken English. Any of the following are nice experience to have, but not essential. Please don’t be put off if you don’t have these: •    Working in high-performance or cloud compute environments. •    Working on machine learning problems (e.g. with frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow). •    Research with health care and/or genomics data. •    Developing software in a small team environment with code review and version control. •    Using agentic AI tools (e.g. from Anthropic and OpenAI) while still retaining your own thinking process (see here for more about how we use AI). What we offer This is an opportunity to be one of the first members of a newly established laboratory led by Professor Jeffrey Barrett, who has over 20 years’ experience leading genomics research teams. You will benefit from hands-on supervision from Professor Barrett as well as active participation in the intellectual environments at both FIMM (genomics and molecular medicine) and the ELLIS Institute (fundamentals of applied AI). Our team has access to biobank data sets which cumulatively include 2 million individuals (FinnGen, UK Biobank, All of Us, Estonian Biobank). We have access to both local supercomputer facilities as well as extensive cloud computing resources. We also routinely generate new ’omics data in samples available from the Finnish biobank network. The position is for a fixed term, with a maximum duration of four years. A trial period of six months will be applied. The salary is based on the salary system of the Finnish universities . The starting salary is typically around 2600-2850 EUR per month, depending on the appointees’ qualifications and experience, and rises gradually as the PhD work progresses. The University of Helsinki offers comprehensive services to its employees, including occupational health care, support in access to high quality sports facilities, and many opportunities for professional development. Standard Finnish pension benefits are provided for university employees. How to apply Please submit your application through the University of Helsinki recruitment system by November 19 , 2026. Your application should include: •    A one-page cover letter describing why you’re interested in this role. Please don’t use AI for this! It’s important to explain in your own voice. •    CV, including publications and github link if applicable •    Contact information for two references For more information regarding the position or the research goals of the group, please contact Jeff at jeffrey.c.barrett(at)helsinki.fi. More information A diverse and equitable study and work culture is important to us. That is why we do our best to promote an inclusive university community. We encourage all qualified applicants from diverse backgrounds to apply for our positions. Click this link to read about accessibility and inclusivity at our University. JOIN US TO BUILD A BETTER WORLD – TOGETHER! #HelsinkiUniCareers The Institute for Molecular Medicine Finland (FIMM) is an international research unit focusing on human genomics and personalized medicine at the Helsinki Institute of Life Science (HiLIFE) of the University of Helsinki - a leading Nordic university with a strong commitment to life science research. As part of Academic Medical Center Helsinki in Meilahti campus FIMM collaborates locally with the Faculty of Medicine, Helsinki University Hospital and National Institute for Health and Welfare. FIMM is part of the Nordic EMBL Partnership for Molecular Medicine, composed of the European Molecular Biology Laboratory (EMBL) and the centres for molecular medicine in Norway, Sweden and Denmark, and the EU-LIFE Community. ELLIS (European Laboratory for Learning and Intelligent Systems) is a major European initiative in AI with a mission to strengthen Europe’s AI landscape by connecting top researchers, attracting talent, and fostering strategic collaborations. ELLIS unites leading machine learning researchers in Europe and operates as a multi-centric, pan-European AI Lab, currently spanning 47 research sites. ELLIS Institute Finland was launched in 2025 and is the second institute in the ELLIS network , partnering with Finnish universities. We develop machine learning through fundamental research, with a particular focus on the fundamentals of applied AI: making machine learning more widely and effectively applicable, and better at working with people. AI for Research is one part of this focus. Our faculty works across a broad range of areas, including data-efficient probabilistic machine learning, generative modelling, amortized inference, interactive and cooperative machine learning, and transformative multidisciplinary collaboration. The institute will have a small number of strategic focus areas and the first one is AI for Health, spearheaded by a project to build a nationwide foundation model to support better decision-making in healthcare. Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 19.11.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Helsinki Institute of Life Science Sub-unit: Institute for Molecular Medicine Finland (FIMM) ID: 5268 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Teaching and research positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CONTACT Data protection Contact us WHY US? Why University of Helsinki Why Finland CAREER SITES Academic careers Expert careers FACULTIES AND UNITS Flamma intranet Faculties and Units © University of Helsinki 2022 × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Advertising Cookies These cookies serve ads that are relevant to your interests. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionality that these third parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Advertising Cookies Show More Details Advertising 