    "https://jobs.helsinki.fi/job/Helsinki-Doctoral-Researcher-in-Archaelogy-or-Geoscience/1375701157/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher in Archaelogy or Geoscience",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher in Archaelogy or Geoscience Job Details | University of Helsinki We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login View all jobs View by category Professors and assistant / associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions Careers Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login VIEW ALL JOBS VIEW BY CATEGORY Professors, assistant and associate professors Teaching and research positions Leadership, specialist and support positions CAREERS Language English Suomi Svenska Profile Employee Login Search by title, unit or a word Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Doctoral Researcher in Archaelogy or Geoscience The Faculty of Humanities at the University of Helsinki and Academy Research Fellow Maria Lahtinen invite applications for the position of Doctoral Researcher in Archaelogy or Geoscience, for a fixed-term position of three years. The position is full-time (fully funded) and will be based within the discipline of Archaeology in the Department of Cultures. The employment will commence on 1 January 2027 or as agreed. Research Project The position is funded by the Research Council of Finland project \"Strontium Isotope Tools to Trace Mobility of Aquatic Diet in the Past, the Present, and the Future (SRTOOL).\" The successful applicant will focus on one of the following research topics: A) Investigating the Origin and Use of Prehistoric Seals Using Strontium Isotope Analysis This research stream focuses on archaeological materials and the application of strontium isotope analysis. The aim is to determine, through the analysis of burned animal bones, where seals were hunted. The project will also explore the significance of seal hunting for prehistoric communities. The research combines scientific and humanities-based approaches. B) Investigating the Use of Strontium Isotope Analysis in Aquatic Materials This research stream seeks to determine the strontium isotope signatures in various regions of the Baltic Sea and Finland's largest lakes and create baseline (isoscape) for the future studies. The project will also investigate whether large-scale temporal variation exists in strontium isotope compositions in major lake systems in the past. This research is primarily natural science-oriented. Main Duties · Conduct doctoral research and prepare a doctoral dissertation. · Produce scientific publications related to the research project. · Complete doctoral studies as part of the PhD programme. · Independently carry out laboratory analyses. · Perform statistical analyses. · Apply GIS methods and software in research. · Collaborate with other members of the research project. · Participate in project activities, including meetings, seminars, workshops, and selected administrative tasks. · Present research results at national and international conferences and other scientific events. Please indicate in your application which of the two research topics you are applying for. The most important qualification is interests on research and the ability and willingness to acquire new skills. Applicants are encouraged to apply even if they do not yet possess all the competencies in jobs listed above. The project leader will work closely with the selected candidate and will contribute complementary expertise to the research. Eligibility and Selection Criteria To meet the basic requirements of the University of Helsinki's Doctoral Programme in the Humanities, applicants must: · Meet the University's language requirements by demonstrating proficiency in Finnish, Swedish, or English. For this position, excellent written and spoken English is required. · Hold a Master's degree or equivalent in a field relevant to the proposed doctoral research. Applicants who are close to completing their Master's degree are also encouraged to apply. Relevant topics can be for example geosciences or archaeological sciences. · Be eligible to pursue doctoral studies at the University of Helsinki. Applicants who do not yet hold the right to pursue doctoral studies must apply for it separately. Continued employment is contingent upon obtaining doctoral study rights within the first six months of employment. What We Offer The position offers an opportunity to work in an inspiring, international, and multidisciplinary research environment. The salary is based on the Finnish university salary system for teaching and research staff at requirement level 2, plus a personal performance component. The starting gross salary is approximately €2,700 per month.The position includes a six-month probationary period. The University of Helsinki offers a comprehensive range of employee benefits, including occupational healthcare services, professional development opportunities, support for research funding applications, and access to library and sports services. Application Instructions Applications must be submitted through the University of Helsinki's online recruitment system using the \"Apply Now\" button. Applicants currently employed by the University of Helsinki should submit their application through the SAP Fiori portal. Please submit the following documents as a single PDF file: · A motivation letter (maximum two pages) describing your interest in the position and outlining relevant experience. · A curriculum vitae, including a list of publications (if applicable). · Two letters of recommendation, including the referees' contact information. Application Deadline 20 November 2026 at 23:59 (Finnish time) Further Information For further information about the position, please contact: Maria Lahtinen Academy Research Fellow maria.lahtinen@helsinki.fi For questions regarding the recruitment process, please contact: recruitment@helsinki.fi The University of Helsinki welcomes applications from individuals of all genders, linguistic and cultural backgrounds, and minority groups. Do you have a helsinki.fi username and a valid employment contract, a grant researcher's contract, a visiting researcher's or visiting professor's contract at the University of Helsinki? Log in here to apply to our open positions. Employee Login Open position Due Date: 20.11.2026 (23.59 Europe/Helsinki time) Unit: Faculty of Humanities Sub-unit: Department of Cultures ID: 5294 Working for the world Science has the power to change the world. Join one of the best research universities in the world – an international community united through bold thinking, science, research, and learning, with over 30,000 students and 8,000 employees. We are defined by our multidisciplinary approach. This, combined with a dedication for cross-border collaboration, gives us our potential to find real solutions and build hope for a better, more sustainable future. We are united by our values – truth, bildung, freedom, and inclusivity – as well as our passion for work that truly matters. Join us: work for the future – work for the world. Any questions? See our recruitment system FAQ Apply now » Find similar jobs: Teaching and research positions Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab.